In the `ExportPopRecordCommand.export` method, there's no logging of success or failure for each broker. It would be helpful to log a message indicating whether the export was successful or if an error occurred.
```java
try {
    if (!dryRun) {
        adminExt.exportPopRecords(brokerAddr, TimeUnit.SECONDS.toMillis(30));
    }
    System.out.printf("Export broker records, " +
        "brokerName=%s, brokerAddr=%s, dryRun=%s%n", brokerName, brokerAddr, dryRun);
} catch (Exception e) {
    System.err.printf("Failed to export broker records, " +
        "brokerName=%s, brokerAddr=%s, dryRun=%s%n%s", brokerName, brokerAddr, dryRun, e.getMessage());
}
```

In the `ExportPopRecordCommand.execute` method, there's no validation to ensure that either 'b' (brokerAddr) or 'c' (clusterName) is provided. If neither option is given, the command will do nothing silently. It would be better to throw an exception or print a usage message.
```java
if (!commandLine.hasOption('b') && !commandLine.hasOption('c')) {
    System.out.println("Either -b brokerAddr or -c clusterName must be specified.");
    return;
}
```

